---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { site, brand } from '../../content/site';
const c = site.en;
const updated = '2 September 2026';
---
<Base c={{ ...c, meta: { title: 'Personal data policy — ' + brand.name, description: 'How we handle the details you leave through the booking form.' } }} lang="en">
  <Nav c={c} />
  <main id="main" class="legal section">
    <div class="shell legal-inner">
      <p class="label">Document</p>
      <h1 class="h2">Personal data policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Version of {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. Who handles your data</h2>
      <p>
The operator is {brand.legalName}, TIN {brand.inn}, OGRN {brand.ogrn},
        at {brand.addressEn}. Reach us on {brand.phone} or at {brand.email}.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <p>
Through the booking form: your name, phone number, the topic you chose and a comment
        if you left one. The form asks for nothing else and collects nothing automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why</h2>
      <p>
One purpose only: to contact you about your enquiry — to call back, clarify details and
        book an appointment. We do not use these details for mailings and do not pass them
        to third parties for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>4. On what basis</h2>
      <p>
On the basis of your consent, given when you send the form. You may withdraw it at any
        time by writing to {brand.email} or calling us. After withdrawal we delete the data
        within 10 working days.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
Enquiries are kept no longer than needed to handle the request and to maintain medical
        records for the periods set by law. After that the data is deleted or anonymised.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
A booking is delivered to our internal work messenger, which only clinic staff handling
        appointments can access. The site is hosted by a provider acting as a processor on
        our instructions.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How it is protected</h2>
      <p>
The connection to the site is encrypted (HTTPS). Access keys for the delivery service are
        stored encrypted on the hosting side and never appear in the site's code.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
You may ask what data we hold, require it to be corrected, blocked or deleted, and
        withdraw your consent. Contact us in any of the ways listed above.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
If this policy changes, the new version appears on this page with a new date.
      </p>

      <p class="legal-back"><a href="/">← Back to the site</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer c={c} />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { padding-top: 130px; }
  .legal-inner { max-width: 720px; }
  .legal-inner .h2 { margin: 14px 0 8px; }
  .legal-meta { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-faint); margin-bottom: 34px; }
  .legal-inner h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 300; font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin: 30px 0 10px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .legal-inner p { color: var(--color-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
  .legal-back { margin-top: 44px; }
  .legal-back a { color: var(--color-accent); text-decoration: none; }
</style>
